# URL of the Keystone app (project management), used by "Ouvrir dans Keystone".
NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYSTONE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Where Codex keeps its local database and uploaded files (default: ./.data).
# CODEX_DATA_DIR=.data
# PostgreSQL server instead of the embedded database (option, docs/postgres.md; where Codex is hosted is not decided).
# Unset (default, local use, Mac app): PGlite in $CODEX_DATA_DIR/pglite. Set: that server, PostgreSQL 18 or later with
# ICU and the pg_trgm extension (created at start unless already there), same migrations, functions and triggers. The
# uploaded files stay in $CODEX_DATA_DIR/files. Codex does not back a server up (npm run backup, restore, export and
# integrity refuse; Administration › Export complet and Intégrité work): use the server's tools (pg_dump). A new server
# database receives CODEX_SEED=minimal unless CODEX_SEED says otherwise.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://codex:password@db.example:5432/codex
# Largest number of connections of one Codex process to that server (default 10, from 2 to 200).
# CODEX_DB_POOL_MAX=10
# Tests only (npm run test:pg): a PostgreSQL 18 server whose user may create databases; each test file gets its own.
# CODEX_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/postgres
# What a new, empty database receives (src/lib/seed-mode.ts), read only when it is empty: demo (default with the
# embedded database, development and Mac app) loads the reference data and the demonstration (fictitious people,
# projects, documents); minimal loads the reference data alone (register, functions, permission matrix, provisional organisation, system actors) and an
# initial administrator (default with DATABASE_URL). A real deployment sets minimal. Any other value stops the server
# (configuration check).
# CODEX_SEED=minimal
# Before applying new migrations to a database that holds data, the server writes a backup of it (as npm run backup,
# into CODEX_BACKUP_DIR) and refuses to migrate when it cannot. off migrates without it (not advised). With DATABASE_URL
# it cannot: the server refuses to migrate until off is set, once the server's own backup is made.
# CODEX_MIGRATION_BACKUP=off

# ── Backups (src/lib/backup-core.mjs, docs/sauvegarde.md) ──
# Archives of the database and of the files it refers to: npm run backup (server stopped) or Administration > Journal
# d'audit > Sauvegardes (server running); npm run restore -- <archive> [--replace] (server stopped). Not encrypted,
# owner-only (0700 / 0600). Default: beside the data directory ($CODEX_DATA_DIR-backups, ./.data-backups), outside it so
# that npm run db:reset leaves them. Must not be inside the database or the files. Where archives should be kept
# (another disk, another machine) and how often to back up are not decided (hosting): nothing is scheduled.
# CODEX_BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/codex
# Rotation keeps the N most recent archives and the latest of each of the last N days (default 7, at least 1).
# The application backs up at most once every 15 minutes, so that a run of clicks cannot push older archives out.
# CODEX_BACKUP_KEEP=7
# The npm commands read these as Next does: the environment, then .env.production.local, .env.local, .env.production,
# .env (next start, Mac app), or with --dev .env.development.local, .env.local, .env.development, .env (next dev).
# Full export (docs/export.md): no variable of its own. Administration › Journal d'audit › Export complet streams the
# archive to a records manager; npm run export (server stopped) writes it beside the data directory
# ($CODEX_DATA_DIR-exports, ./.data-exports) unless --out says where. Unencrypted, drafts included: keep it safe.

# ── Integration API (docs/api.md) ──
# Bearer token of POST /api/import (migration tool). Unset: the import API is disabled (503).
# At least 32 varied characters, e.g. openssl rand -base64 32: a shorter one (such as the placeholder below) stops the
# server in production (CODEX_CONFIG_CHECK, below).
# CODEX_IMPORT_TOKEN=change-me
# Bearer token of POST /api/integrations/vigie (Vigie decisions webhook). Unset: the webhook is disabled (503). Same rule.
# VIGIE_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=change-me
# Vigie API; while unset, Vigie decisions can be simulated from Codex by a records manager.
# VIGIE_API_URL=http://localhost:3200/api
# URL of the Vigie app, used by "Ouvrir dans Vigie".
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VIGIE_URL=http://localhost:3200

# ── File storage (src/lib/storage.ts) ──
# local (default): files under $CODEX_DATA_DIR/files. sharepoint: a SharePoint library driven by Codex through
# Microsoft Graph (app-only); only the file, its name and its version go to SharePoint, all metadata stays in Codex.
# CODEX_STORAGE=local
# CODEX_SP_TENANT_ID=
# CODEX_SP_CLIENT_ID=
# CODEX_SP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# CODEX_SP_DRIVE_ID=
# Orphan files (src/lib/orphans.ts, Administration > Journal d'audit): a stored file no working version refers to is
# only counted, and removed by a records manager, once written, linked or moved more than this many whole hours ago
# (default 24, at least 1), so that an upload in progress is never touched. SharePoint orphans are listed, never removed.
# CODEX_ORPHAN_GRACE_HOURS=24

# ── Files entering Codex: formats, size, virus scan (src/lib/filetypes.ts, src/lib/antivirus.ts) ──
# Checked for every way in: new document, working version, copy of a template, POST /api/import.
# Largest file, in MB, the same for every way in (default 50; at most 250 with CODEX_STORAGE=sharepoint). Read when
# the server starts: it also sets the request size of the Server Actions (next.config.ts). Replaces
# CODEX_IMPORT_MAX_MB, no longer read.
# CODEX_MAX_FILE_MB=50
# Extensions admitted, the whole list, comma-separated (default: documents, spreadsheets, presentations, Visio,
# Project, e-mails, images, MP4, drawings and models, JSON, XML; archives such as zip only when listed here).
# Executables, scripts, web pages, SVG, disk images and Office extensions with macros are refused even when listed,
# and so are VBA macros whatever the extension (README, "Fichiers déposés").
# CODEX_FILE_EXTENSIONS=pdf,doc,docx,dotx,odt,rtf,txt,xls,xlsx,xltx,ods,csv,ppt,pptx,potx,odp,vsdx,mpp,msg,eml,png,jpg,jpeg,gif,webp,tif,tiff,heic,mp4,dwg,dxf,step,stp,iges,igs,ifc,stl,json,xml
# clamd's address, to scan every file before it is stored: host:port (TCP, port 3310 by default) or the absolute
# path of its Unix socket. Unset (default, local use, Mac app): no scan, said in the server log and in
# Administration > Journal d'audit.
# In clamd.conf, set StreamMaxLength and MaxFileSize (100M by default since ClamAV 0.105, 25M before) and MaxScanSize
# (400M, 100M before) to at least CODEX_MAX_FILE_MB, and AlertExceedsMax yes: without it, clamd answers OK for a file
# beyond MaxFileSize or MaxScanSize without scanning it. A file beyond these limits is refused as such.
# CODEX_CLAMD=127.0.0.1:3310
# CODEX_CLAMD=/run/clamav/clamd.ctl
# Longest wait for clamd's answer, in milliseconds (default 30000).
# CODEX_CLAMD_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# A file clamd could not scan (unreachable, timed out, error, beyond its limits): refuse (default) or accept (stored
# unscanned, logged).
# CODEX_CLAMD_ON_ERROR=refuse

# ── HTTP security headers (src/lib/security-headers.ts, src/proxy.ts) ──
# Set to 1 only when Codex is served over HTTPS (behind a TLS reverse proxy): adds Strict-Transport-Security
# (one year, this host only) and upgrade-insecure-requests. Leave unset locally and in the Mac app (plain HTTP):
# HSTS on localhost would force HTTPS on every local app.
# CODEX_HTTPS=1

# ── Rate limiting (src/lib/ratelimit.ts) ──
# Requests allowed per key, as "N" (per minute) or "N/<duration>" (30s, 1m, 15m, 1h); "0" or "off" lifts a limit.
# Beyond, 429 with Retry-After. Counters live in memory, in the one server process (see README).
# Set to 1 only when a reverse proxy in front of Codex writes X-Forwarded-For (replaces it, or appends the address it
# sees) and clients cannot reach Codex without it. Unset (default, local use, Mac app): the client may write that header
# itself, so its address never holds anyone else back: the right token always goes through, the registry is not
# limited and the browser routes count per user only.
# CODEX_TRUST_PROXY=1
# Lifts every limit below:
# CODEX_RATE_LIMIT=off
# POST /api/import and POST /api/integrations/vigie, per client address, counted once the token is checked:
# CODEX_RATE_IMPORT=600/1m
# CODEX_RATE_VIGIE=600/1m
# Tokens refused on those two, per client address: beyond, wrong tokens get 429 instead of 401; with
# CODEX_TRUST_PROXY=1, the address then waits even with the right token:
# CODEX_RATE_TOKEN_FAILURES=20/15m
# GET /api/registry, per client address, with CODEX_TRUST_PROXY=1 only:
# CODEX_RATE_REGISTRY=300/1m
# Stored files and approval records, then CSV exports and the full export, per user (as resolved from the session, not
# the raw cookie), and per client address too with CODEX_TRUST_PROXY=1:
# CODEX_RATE_FILES=600/1m
# CODEX_RATE_EXPORTS=30/1m
# Server Actions that write, per user:
# CODEX_RATE_WRITES=120/1m

# ── Technical log, health route, configuration check (src/lib/log.ts, src/lib/config-check.ts, docs/exploitation.md) ──
# The technical log goes to the server's output (stdout, stderr for warnings and errors), apart from the audit trail:
# one entry per line, with the request's identifier (X-Request-Id), never a token, a cookie or a document's content.
# Format: json (one object per line, for a log collector) or pretty (readable). Default: json in production (next
# start, Mac app), pretty otherwise (next dev).
# CODEX_LOG_FORMAT=json
# Lowest level written: debug, info (default), warn, error, silent. GET /api/health is logged at debug when it answers 200.
# CODEX_LOG_LEVEL=info
# What a configuration error found at start does (CODEX_STORAGE unknown, SharePoint half set up, integration token
# shorter than 32 characters, Vigie or Keystone address that is no http(s) URL, CODEX_CLAMD unreadable, data folder
# not writable…): strict refuses to start (exit code 1), warn logs it and starts. Default: strict in production, warn
# in development. The default configuration (no variable) has no error: local use and the Mac app start as before.
# CODEX_CONFIG_CHECK=strict
